WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:04.351
With about 11,000,000 open job roles in the United States alone,

00:00:04.351 --> 00:00:08.529
organizations are struggling to find qualified candidates at a pace that's fast enough.

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:12.966
And with the growth in social media and other publicly available personal data,

00:00:12.966 --> 00:00:15.819
it's difficult to address bias in the hiring process.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:19.630
So let's tackle these issues by addressing two key questions.

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:24.999
First, how can you find candidates who have the right skills for your job opening and your business?

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:29.589
And second, how can you connect with these candidates in a quick and more streamlined way?

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.030
Well, don't worry, because this is where IBM and ThisWay Global come in.

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:40.438
IBM Watson Orchestrate and ThisWay Global combine the power of your Watson Orchestrate digital employee, or "digey",

00:00:40.438 --> 00:00:43.360
with ThisWay Global's diversity sourcing and matching engine.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:46.810
So you can find qualified candidates from a diverse talent pool.

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:48.170
Here's how it works.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.099
First, let's find qualified candidates for the job.

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:54.279
In this case, the job descriptions reside in Box.

00:00:54.670 --> 00:01:00.262
Just select the job you need to hire for, and your digey connects with ThisWay Global's candidate sourcing technology

00:01:00.262 --> 00:01:02.979
to provide you with potentially hundreds of matches.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:05.708
You can also filter for specific locations.

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:10.569
Here we're pulling candidates from Denver, Colorado through ThisWay Global's Discover Service.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:14.499
Once you have your list, you can easily save the file for future reference.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:18.670
Now you can contact the candidates you selected using the saved data.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.189
Let's encourage them to apply for the opportunity.

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:26.973
Note that the email comes from your email address so the message is less likely to be flagged by spam filters.

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:30.920
You can even use custom templates and personalize for your audience.

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:35.560
Your digey curates and sends the email to your selected candidates, including a link to apply.

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:37.490
That was fast and easy, right?

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:40.776
But what about increasing the diversity of your talent pool?

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:45.939
Traditional hiring processes can include the evaluation of candidates based on their social profiles.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:48.897
This can trigger conscious and unconscious bias

00:01:48.897 --> 00:01:52.308
- maybe caused by something as simple as someone's picture or name.

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:59.197
ThisWay's technology empowers your digey to surface diverse candidates by redacting data that may influence biased decisions.

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:04.079
Here, check out how potential bias is redacted from the resume screening process.

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:07.850
This is key to delivering diverse and qualified candidates.

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:09.869
So to wrap this up,

00:02:09.869 --> 00:02:16.484
Watson Orchestrate and ThisWay Global combine the value of digeys with an engine that can help you increase the diversity of your talent pool

00:02:16.484 --> 00:02:18.699
and identify qualified candidates.

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:22.914
You get assistance from your digey to find qualified candidates with the right skills for the role,

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:24.909
A streamlined way to contact candidates,

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:29.229
and most importantly, knowing you've helped to reduce bias during the hiring process.

00:02:29.770 --> 00:02:30.700
Thanks for watching.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:32.771
To learn more, please click on the link.

